[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | incomplete decimal exponent | `1e`, `1e+`, `1e-`, `1e+x`, `0.5e` | the `e…` is not consumed; the mantissa still converts (`1e` → `1.0`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `inf` / `infinity` | `inf`, `INF`, `iNf`, `-inf`, `infinity`, `InFiNiTy`, `infinityx` | infinity, sign applied |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | **partial** `infinity` | `infi`, `infin`, `infini`, `infinit`, `-infinit` | matching failure → `00000000`; glibc cannot back out of a partial suffix match |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `inf` followed by other text | `inf1`, `infz`, `inf inity` | infinity (`inf` alone matched) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `nan` | `nan`, `NaN`, `-nan`, `+nan` | quiet NaN `0000c07f`; `-nan` sets the sign → `0000c0ff` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `nan(payload)` | `nan(123)`, `nan(0x7)`, `-nan(abc)`, `nan(` | payload is **not** parsed by `%f`; result is the same `0000c07f` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | hex float | `0x1p3`, `0X1p-3`, `0x.8p1`, `0x1.8`, `0x123456789abcdef1p0`, `0xABCDEF` | C99 hex form accepted |
